	abstract = {Model predictive control ({MPC}) is used to solve the economic dispatch problem in an isolated power system with distributed energy resources ({DERs}), such as renewable energy resources (wind, solar), battery energy storage subsystems and fossil fueled generators (diesel generators). The problem is formulated as a multi-objective optimization problem with the quadratic cost function and subject to some linear constraints. The proposed optimization problem is converted to standard quadratic programming and finally to feedback {MPC}. Developed optimal coordination of {DERs} has been implemented and is demonstrated on the simple example. © 2019 {IEEE}.},
