	abstract = {In order to obtain global optimization of the microgrid and consider the loss characteristics of the battery, a multi-objective optimization model, using minimum comprehensive cost, maximum environmental benefit, and minimum battery depletion as its objectives, was established. An improved multiple objective particle swarm optimization ({MOPSO}) algorithm was introduced, which obtains better convergence and population diversity by adopting the strategies of adaptively selecting global optimum and maintaining the population diversity with mutation operator. Meanwhile, it uses the Latin hypercube sampling method to generate the original particles with wider distribution, which would decrease the possibility to be trapped in the local optimum. Simulation on a certain microgrid shows effectiveness of the methodology proposed by this paper. © 2016 Chin. Soc. for Elec. Eng.},
