	abstract = {The distributed energy supply system based on multi-energy complementarity is currently a research hotspot in the field of energy engineering, and the key issue faced by this system is operation optimization. The reasonable configuration or not directly affects the economic benefits and operational efficiency of the system. This article focuses on this key issue faced by distributed energy supply systems with multiple complementary energy sources. Taking a cultural tourism park as the research object, considering factors such as economic indicators, energy consumption, and carbon emissions, a multi-objective optimization model for distributed energy supply systems with multiple complementary energy sources is established by gradually decomposing and introducing hourly energy constraints. Experiments have shown that compared to traditional systems, this model can achieve hourly operation optimization and has good economic efficiency and energy-saving and emission-reduction benefits. Therefore, it provides a good reference and reference for the energy supply and comprehensive energy planning of multi-energy complementary distributed energy supply systems. © The Institution of Engineering \& Technology 2023.},
