	doi = {10.1109/ICNEPE64067.2024.10860367},
	abstract = {This paper addresses the issue of poor controllability of off-grid hydrogen production from renewable energy sources, which makes it difficult to meet hydrogen load demands. A multi-objective planning method combining various hydrogen production technologies is proposed. By integrating water electrolysis hydrogen production, biomass gasification hydrogen production, and natural gas reforming hydrogen production, the utilization rate of hydrogen production by-products is improved, and the controllability of hydrogen production is enhanced, achieving complementary advantages among hydrogen production technologies. Additionally, the paper describes the characteristics of three types of hydrogen load demands, enhancing the coordination capabilities of the production-storage-use processes. Finally, simulation examples verify the rationality of the proposed hydrogen production system.  © 2024 {IEEE}.},
