	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85182931396&doi=10.1109%2fSGES59720.2023.10367022&partnerID=40&md5=40d6e2d6f805c5462e7c6046191b170f},
	doi = {10.1109/SGES59720.2023.10367022},
	abstract = {A microgrid energy optimization management method with an improved ant-lion optimization algorithm is proposed for the multi-objective optimal microgrid configuration, making the microgrid operation more efficient, economical, and reasonable. A two-tier energy optimization management is established, with the optimization objectives of micro point network operation cost-benefit, active power loss, and carbon emission. The upper layer uses a fuzzy management system to determine the microgrid operation mode, and the lower layer uses an improved ant-lion optimization algorithm to optimize energy management. Adaptive weights are then invoked to improve the antlion diversity and convergence accuracy. The rationality and effectiveness of the energy management method, the optimization model, and the improved antlion algorithm in this paper are verified by comparing the gray wolf and whale algorithms.  © 2023 {IEEE}.},
