	doi = {10.3390/su9010117},
	abstract = {Recently, the off-grid smart house has been attracting attention in Japan for considering global warming. Moreover, the selling price of surplus power from the renewable energy system by Feed-In Tariff ({FIT}) has declined. Therefore, this paper proposes an off-grid smart house with the introduced Photovoltaic ({PV}) system, Solar Collector ({SC}) system, {HotWater} Heat Pump ({HWHP}), fixed battery and Electric Vehicle ({EV}). In this research, a multi-objective optimization problem is considered to minimize the introduced capacity and shortage of the power supply in the smart house. It can perform the electric power procurement from the {EV} charging station for the compensation of a shortage of power supply. From the simulation results, it is shown that the shortage of the power supply can be reduced by the compensation of the {EV} power. Furthermore, considering the uncertainty for {PV} output power, reliable simulation results can be obtained. © 2017 by the authors.},
