	abstract = {Electrical power networks can be improved both technically and economically through the inclusion of distributed generator ({DG}) units, which may include renewable energy resources. This work uses multi-objective optimization by evolutionary computing, with power flow calculations and multi-dimensional results analysis, to investigate a method of defining optimal deployment of {DG} units. The results indicate that the method used is a feasible one for designing deployment of {DG} units in terms of type, number, and location. © 2015, Emergent Publications. All rights reserved.},
