	abstract = {To realize safe，clean and reliable energy supply in remote regions，integrating clean energy（such as wind，solar，and biogas resources）and constructing integrated energy microgrids（{IEM}）with renewable energy as the main body is one of the important ways to promote low-carbon，safe and efficient development of power systems in remote regions. Therefore，this paper presents a multiobjective programming method for {IEM} planning considering the coordinated operation of wind，solar，biogas，and energy storages. Firstly，based on the in-depth analysis of operation and correlation characteristics of various energy conversion equipment in the {IEM}，the mathematical models for wind，solar，biogas，and energy storage are established. Then，with the minimum system cost and the maximum utilization of renewable energy as the objectives，the multi-objective planning model of {IEMs} is proposed，while considering constraints for both planning and operation stages. Finally，the {NSGA}-域 algorithm is introduced to solve the proposed problem，and the simulation results verify the effectiveness of the proposed model. © 2023 Science Press. All rights reserved.},
