	url = {https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85082463877&doi=10.13334%2fj.0258-8013.pcsee.180824&partnerID=40&md5=e930965e6bd968bfd77a25433bbdb78e},
	doi = {10.13334/j.0258-8013.pcsee.180824},
	abstract = {Microgrid energy management system ({MGEMS}) is the basis that guarantees efficient operation of microgrid, and operation optimization algorithm is the core of {MGEMS}. This paper presented a fully distributed multi-objective optimization algorithm for microgrid based on potential game to face the development tendency of intelligence and openness, especially self-interest, autonomy, and plug-and-play of individuals. The different component units (including load) were treated as independent decision-making entities, and build multi-objective optimization models according to various self-seeking objectives. By introducing potential game, a distributed optimization game model consisting of interaction among resources, storages, and loads was built. Further, by integrating {MOPSO} and constrained domination principle, a distributed iterative method was developed to solve this game model. Simulation results show that, the self-interest and intelligence of individuals are fully reflected; economic, environmental, and satisfaction goals are coordinated; distributed individual interests and global interests are unified. The feasibility and validity of the proposed algorithm are verified. © 2020 Chin. Soc. for Elec. Eng.},
